# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. A shell script that comes back with CRLF has
# "#!/bin/sh\r" as its shebang, which is not a valid interpreter path on Unix,
# so the script fails to execute. For .githooks/ that would silently disable
# the embargo guard on a fresh clone, which is the exact failure mode the
# tracked hook exists to prevent.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
